docs/APPLICATIONS.md:3:This document describes the user-facing applications in the Complaint Generator system, including the command-line interface (CLI) and web server.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:93:| `!export-complaint` | Build a court-style complaint draft and render document artifacts such as DOCX and PDF, then print a compact summary and the full package JSON |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:187:To launch the same review/document surface with Hugging Face router inference as the active backend:
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:198:- `/document` for the browser-based formal complaint builder and preview surface
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:201:- `/api/documents/formal-complaint` for building formal complaint drafts and rendering DOCX/PDF artifacts
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:202:- `/api/documents/download` for downloading generated DOCX/PDF artifacts from the managed output directory
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:205:The formal complaint endpoint also accepts agentic optimization controls, including `optimization_provider`, `optimization_model_name`, and `optimization_llm_config`, so the browser builder or external callers can route optimization traffic through the same Hugging Face router endpoint when needed. The `/document` builder exposes both simple router fields and an advanced JSON editor for `optimization_llm_config`, with the simple fields overriding matching top-level keys for quick experimentation.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:211:  --db-path statefiles/claim_support.duckdb \
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:215:  --db-path statefiles/claim_support.duckdb
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:229:| `/claim-support-review` | Operator review dashboard for claim support, targeted question recommendations, testimony intake, pasted or uploaded document intake, parse-quality signals, follow-up execution, recent follow-up history, and manual-review resolution | HTML template (claim_support_review.html) |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:237:| `/document` | Formal complaint builder and preview surface for court-style pleading drafts | HTML template (document.html) |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:245:| `/api/claim-support/review` | Claim-element review packet for operator or UI workflows | JSON payload with `claim_coverage_matrix`, `claim_coverage_summary`, `claim_support_gaps`, `claim_contradiction_candidates`, optional `support_summary`, `claim_overview`, `follow_up_plan`, compact `follow_up_plan_summary`, and persisted `follow_up_history` or `follow_up_history_summary`; authority-targeted follow-up summaries can also expose compact legal-retrieval warning aggregates such as `search_warning_count`, `warning_family_counts`, `warning_code_counts`, `hf_dataset_id_counts`, and `search_warning_summary`; coverage payloads include compact support-lineage packet summaries for archived captures and authority fallbacks; `follow_up_execution` remains compatibility-only |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:248:| `/api/claim-support/save-document` | Persist pasted document text for the current claim-support review context through the shared evidence parse, chunk, and graph pipeline | JSON payload with `document_result`, `recorded`, and optional `post_save_review` using the standard review contract |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:249:| `/api/claim-support/upload-document` | Persist an uploaded file for the current claim-support review context through the shared evidence parse, chunk, and graph pipeline | Multipart form response with `document_result`, `recorded`, and optional `post_save_review` using the standard review contract |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:251:| `/api/documents/formal-complaint` | Formal complaint export endpoint for court-style pleading drafts | JSON payload with the structured draft, generated artifact paths, selected output formats, generation timestamp, and claim-level drafting-readiness or support-summary context used by the builder preview |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:252:| `/api/documents/download` | Download a generated complaint artifact from the managed output directory | Generated DOCX or PDF file response |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:281:- `claim_support_gaps`: unresolved-element diagnostics keyed by claim type.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:283:- `question_recommendations`: targeted operator-facing question packets keyed by claim type, grouped around contradiction resolution, testimony clarification, document requests, or authority clarification.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:286:- `document_artifacts`: persisted dashboard-ingested evidence artifacts keyed by claim type, including parse, chunk, fact, and graph previews for uploaded or pasted materials.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:287:- `document_summary`: compact document-artifact counts keyed by claim type, including linked-element counts, total chunks, total facts, graph-ready counts, low-quality parse counts, and parse-status mix.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:328:##### `/api/documents/formal-complaint` - Formal Complaint Export
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:332:The browser UI for this workflow is available at `/document`, which submits to this endpoint and renders artifact download links, section-level drafting readiness, claim-level filing warnings, compact claim-level source context, guardrail summaries, managed artifact provenance, and the generated pleading text from the response payload.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:334:DOCX generation uses `python-docx` when that optional package is installed. In slim deployments where the package is unavailable, the document pipeline still emits valid DOCX containers with the pleading and affidavit text, section headings, grouped factual allegation headings, readiness-driven open gaps, and claim-support handoff content preserved for operator review. PDF, TXT, checklist, and packet artifacts continue through their native renderers.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:344:  "enable_agentic_optimization": true,
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:345:  "optimization_max_iterations": 2,
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:346:  "optimization_target_score": 0.9,
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:347:  "optimization_provider": "huggingface_router",
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:348:  "optimization_model_name": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-480B-A35B-Instruct",
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:349:  "optimization_llm_config": {
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:362:- `enable_agentic_optimization`: runs a post-knowledge-graph refinement loop before artifact rendering.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:363:- `optimization_max_iterations` / `optimization_target_score`: bounds the loop and stopping threshold.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:364:- `optimization_provider` / `optimization_model_name`: selects the routed model used by the actor and critic prompts.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:365:- `optimization_llm_config`: optional provider-specific router overrides such as `base_url`, headers, timeouts, or nested routing settings. In the `/document` UI, the advanced JSON editor is merged with the simple router fields, and the simple fields win on conflicts.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:366:- `optimization_persist_artifacts`: stores the optimization trace through the IPFS adapter and surfaces the resulting CID in the response.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:368:When the `/document` UI is used, the generated preview also renders a compact optimization summary with router availability, router usage diagnostics, upstream optimizer metadata, stage-level provider selection, packet projection counts, initial/final critic review summaries, routed provider/model/source details, trace status, and section-history lines so operators can review the refinement loop without opening the raw JSON payload.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:370:Minimal TXT-only optimization request:
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:378:  "enable_agentic_optimization": true,
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:379:  "optimization_max_iterations": 1,
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:380:  "optimization_target_score": 0.9,
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:431:curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/documents/formal-complaint \
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:480:- `document_builder_summary`: browser-oriented support and export summary generated by the document API. It includes section support statuses, source-family/artifact-family/content-origin counts, W10.2 guardrail warning and blocker counts, guardrail warning-type counts, managed output directory metadata, downloadable artifact counts, and document grounding metrics.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:485:- `review_intent`: top-level server-rendered review focus chosen from the current readiness warnings so the document builder can restore the most relevant dashboard context without relying only on browser-local history.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:486:- `artifacts.docx.path`: filesystem path to the generated DOCX document when requested.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:487:- `artifacts.pdf.path`: filesystem path to the generated PDF document when requested.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:489:- `artifacts.affidavit_docx.path`, `artifacts.affidavit_pdf.path`, `artifacts.affidavit_txt.path`: filesystem paths to the generated affidavit companion documents when the matching output formats are requested.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:491:- `document_optimization`: present only when optimization is enabled. The current payload includes `status`, `method`, `optimizer_backend`, `initial_score`, `final_score`, `iteration_count`, `accepted_iterations`, `optimized_sections`, `artifact_cid`, `trace_storage`, `trace_download_url`, `trace_view_url`, `router_status`, `router_usage`, `upstream_optimizer`, `intake_status`, `intake_constraints`, `packet_projection`, and `section_history`.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:496:##### `/api/documents/download` - Generated Artifact Download
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:500:##### `/api/documents/optimization-trace` - Persisted Optimization Trace Replay
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:502:GET this endpoint with the `cid` returned in `document_optimization.artifact_cid` or use `document_optimization.trace_download_url` directly when you want the application to fetch the persisted optimization trace through the IPFS adapter and return the decoded JSON payload.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:504:##### `/document/optimization-trace` - Optimization Trace Viewer
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:506:GET this page with a `cid` query parameter, or use `document_optimization.trace_view_url`, when you want a browser-friendly audit view that loads the persisted optimization trace and renders intake blockers, contradiction summaries, review scores, iteration history, and the raw JSON trace in one place.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:508:This route only serves files from the managed generated-documents directory and rejects requests outside that boundary.
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:585:| `claim_support_review.html` | Operator dashboard for claim review and follow-up execution |
docs/APPLICATIONS.md:588:| `document.html` | Document viewer/editor (WYSIWYG) |
