docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:5:This report documents the performance profiling of `OntologyGenerator.generate_ontology()` on a large 10k-token legal document to identify bottlenecks and hot paths in the rule-based extraction pipeline.
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:37:Batch 227 profiled a smaller document (48.6 KB ≈ 6,600 tokens):
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:200:**Recommendation**: For large documents (>10K tokens), use `RULE_BASED` for initial extraction, then selectively apply `LLM_FALLBACK` to high-value or ambiguous entities.
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:209:- ✅ Optimization recommendations documented
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:213:The profiling reveals that **regex pattern matching dominates execution time** (54% in `re.Pattern.search()`, 70% cumulative in `_promote_person_entities()`). The three high-impact optimizations (pre-compile patterns, optimize person promotion, cache results) could reduce execution time by **70-80%** (from 165 ms to ~30-50 ms).
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:215:**Current performance (165 ms for 10K tokens) is acceptable for most use cases**, but the sub-linear scaling suggests that documents >50K tokens will require optimization.
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:221:4. Re-profile after optimizations to validate improvements
docs/PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md:229:- `PROFILING_BATCH_262_ANALYSIS.md` - This analysis document
