docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:45:- `Docket Overview`: case caption, court, parties, filings count, retrieved documents count, OCR/indexing status, and missing documents.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:55:Each document card should show:
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:65:Each document viewer should support:
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:71:- "Ask about this page/document" chat handoff.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:80:- Source documents and page/snippet references.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:83:- Missing documents or unindexed documents that could change the answer.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:84:- A safe next action, such as "review document 14 attachment 2" or "OCR is missing for this exhibit."
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:89:- `Ask selected documents`
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:100:2. Add document inventory UI backed by the existing packaged docket/operator dashboard data.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:101:3. Add per-document enrichment status fields for OCR, text extraction, BM25, vector count, KG, citation extraction, and formal logic.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:103:5. Add document viewer handoffs into chatbot prompts with source scope preserved.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:105:7. Add Playwright coverage for docket overview, document selection, annotation, label assignment, and scoped chat handoff.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:110:The latest Docket-to-chat screenshot review narrows the next implementation slice to source-grounded document chat and first-class annotations. The Docket lane is now visible enough to anchor the workflow, so the next slice should not expand the dashboard broadly. It should make one selected document trustworthy and reusable.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:114:- Replace any raw internal route-index start screen with a small goal-based case hub: start/resume complaint, respond to a docket document, review documents, and ask the case assistant.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:116:- Add legal-safety framing before any draft generation: the tool organizes facts and drafts documents, but does not provide legal advice.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:118:- Replace opaque readiness scores with criteria chips that name missing facts, documents, deadlines, citations, or source support.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:123:- A persistent chat scope banner that says whether the assistant is answering from the whole docket, selected documents, one document, one page, or one annotation.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:124:- A selected-document source panel beside chat with title, document type, source/provenance, labels, extracted text preview, and citation targets.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:129:- A plain-language document readiness summary that collapses OCR, text extraction, BM25, vector, knowledge graph, citation, and formal-logic statuses into one readable state.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:130:- One readiness-based primary action per selected document, with secondary actions visually demoted.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:134:- One canonical selected-document card on mobile, with repeated metadata and technical details collapsed behind disclosures.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:145:- Complex multi-document answer synthesis until single-document citations and save actions are reliable.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:147:The first acceptance test should follow one document end to end:
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:149:1. Select a docket document.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:154:6. Return to Docket and see the annotation/deadline reflected on the document.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:162:- `artifacts/ui-audit-docket-plan-review-20260420/screenshots/02-document-chat-context.png`
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:167:- `artifacts/ui-audit-docket-plan-review-20260422/screenshots/02-document-chat-current.png`
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:174:- `artifacts/ui-audit-docket-plan-review-20260425/screenshots/02-document-chat-desktop.png`
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:181:The four-image bundle review hung, while the single-screen document-chat review completed through `multimodal_router` using `codex_cli`. The audit harness should therefore default to one-surface-at-a-time review until bundle execution has reliable timeouts and partial-artifact reporting.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:185:The April 25 single-surface reviews again completed through `multimodal_router` using `codex_cli`. They confirmed the same desktop repairs and added a mobile-first gate: the selected document must fit into one canonical mobile card, expose only two or three high-priority chips before a disclosure, keep one primary action reachable, and dedupe repeated document/status blocks before implementation begins.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:187:The April 25 refresh review completed five page-level `codex_cli` multimodal reviews for the dashboard hub, intake chat, workspace Docket, claim-support Review, and document builder. It adds one more precondition: the first layperson screen cannot be a long internal link index. It needs a goal-based case hub before Docket, annotations, Review, Draft, and chatbot surfaces will feel coherent.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:193:- A docket operator can see whether every document has been downloaded, OCRed, text extracted, indexed, and enriched.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:194:- Selecting a document makes its provenance, text, labels, annotations, and analysis status visible without leaving the workspace.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:196:- Mobile Docket shows selected document title, readiness, nearest deadline or no-deadline state, and one primary action without repeated cards.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:197:- Playwright captures homepage, complaint workspace, docket overview, document viewer, annotations, labels, chat, and package/export surfaces.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:231:The current UI has a coherent staged workflow, but the screenshots reinforce that the surface is still too vertically dense for layperson legal work. The homepage is the clearest screen because it shows only a few choices and readiness signals. The intake, evidence, review, draft, and integrations screens become long operational documents, which makes the next safe action harder to find.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:235:- The homepage should become a package capability entry point, not only a complaint generator hero. It should expose four plain-language cards: guided intake, resume complaint/workspace, open docket/document dataset, and profile/personal information.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:237:- The evidence and review surfaces contain the right ideas, but the page length suggests that document upload, evidence labeling, support matrix, and proof-gap workbench should be separate subsections inside the same workspace.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:239:- The current screenshots do not yet show a first-class docket document viewer. Docket review, annotation, labeling, and document chat should therefore be implemented as a separate Docket lane instead of being buried inside Evidence.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:247:- `Open Docket Dataset`: opens an existing docket/complaint dataset where the user can inspect filings, analyze documents, annotate pages/spans, label evidence, and ask grounded questions.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:258:The next implementation should not try to finish every dashboard. The highest-value slice is a docket document workspace that can make one document trustworthy and reusable.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:262:- Docket Overview with filing/document counts, OCR/indexing status, missing documents, and next best action.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:263:- Document Inventory with document type, source, docket number, page count, OCR status, text extraction status, labels, annotation count, and enrichment status.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:264:- Document Viewer with selected document metadata, page/text preview, OCR confidence, and source provenance.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:266:- Scoped Ask panel with modes: whole docket, selected documents, this document, this page, this annotation.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:274:- Complex multi-document synthesis before single-document citation and save flows are reliable.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:278:The document chatbot should never look like a general legal advice box. It should always show scope and grounding.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:282:- Current scope: whole docket, selected documents, one document, one page, or one annotation.
docs/LAYPERSON_DOCKET_WORKSPACE_UI_UX_PLAN.md:283:- Source panel: selected document title, type, source/provenance, labels, extracted text preview, and citation targets.
